NSXML: a namespace declaration supplied via -addAttribute: corrupts the heap

A prefixed namespace declaration added to an element as an attribute --
[el addAttribute:[NSXMLNode attributeWithName:@"xmlns:rd" stringValue:...]] --
corrupts the heap on release of the enclosing NSXMLDocument, aborting the
process in glibc's allocator within a few build/serialise/release cycles
("malloc_consolidate(): unaligned fastbin chunk detected", in whatever later
allocation looks next). A self-contained Foundation-only reproduction is in
nsxml-xmlns-attribute-teardown.m beside this patch.

Root cause: -[NSXMLNode setName:] on an attribute whose qualified name is
"xmlns:rd" calls xmlSplitQName2, gets prefix "xmlns" + local "rd", and then --
because it treats "xmlns" as an ordinary prefix -- manufactures a namespace
node with the reserved prefix "xmlns" and a NULL href. "xmlns" and "xml" are
reserved: "xmlns:rd" declares the prefix rd, it is not an attribute in a
namespace named "xmlns". The manufactured node is malformed, and its teardown
across the private detached documents -detach creates (one per element wrapper
as the autorelease pool drains after the document is released) writes through
freed chunks. Declaring the same namespace through -addNamespace: never
crashes; keeping the documents alive never crashes; only a *prefixed*
declaration added as an attribute, on a released document, reaches the fault.

This changes two things:

  1. -[NSXMLNode setName:] no longer resolves or manufactures a namespace for
     the reserved "xmlns"/"xml" prefixes; it keeps the qualified name literal.
     libxml prints an unnamespaced attribute by its full name, so a bare
     "xmlns:rd" attribute still serialises as xmlns:rd="...".

  2. -[NSXMLElement addAttribute:] registers a "xmlns:prefix" attribute as a
     real namespace (the -addNamespace: path, which never crashed) rather than
     as an attribute, so prefixed descendants resolve against a proper
     declaration and print with their prefix. The default declaration
     ("xmlns", no prefix) is left as an attribute -- it never took the
     reserved-prefix path and never provoked the fault.

Serialisation is unchanged except that a prefixed xmlns declaration, now a
real namespace, prints before a co-located default-xmlns attribute rather than
after it (declaration order is not significant). The gnustep-base NSXML test
suite (NSXMLNode / NSXMLDocument / NSXMLElement, 420 tests) passes unchanged.

Applies to current master with `patch -p1` (git apply may need --3way or a
trivial rebase depending on nearby churn); developed and tested against the
gnustep/libs-base tree current in early 2026.

diff --git a/Source/NSXMLElement.m b/Source/NSXMLElement.m
index 7484209..6797862 100644
--- a/Source/NSXMLElement.m
+++ b/Source/NSXMLElement.m
@@ -253,6 +253,30 @@ GS_PRIVATE_INTERNAL(NSXMLElement)
 		  format: @"Tried to add attribute to multiple parents."];
     }
 
+  /* A prefixed namespace declaration supplied as an attribute --
+   * "xmlns:prefix" -- is not an ordinary attribute: it declares a namespace
+   * on this element.  Register it as a real namespace rather than storing it
+   * as an attribute.  Doing otherwise builds a namespace node with the
+   * reserved prefix "xmlns" and a NULL href (see -[NSXMLNode setName:]) whose
+   * teardown corrupts the heap when the enclosing document is released, and
+   * leaves prefixed descendants unable to resolve against a proper
+   * declaration.  The serialisation is unchanged: a real namespace prints as
+   * xmlns:prefix="href" just as the attribute did, and prefixed elements
+   * bound to it now print with their prefix.  The default declaration
+   * ("xmlns", no prefix) is left as an attribute: it does not take the
+   * reserved-prefix path in -setName: and does not provoke the fault. */
+  {
+    NSString *aname = [attribute name];
+
+    if ([aname hasPrefix: @"xmlns:"] && [aname length] > 6)
+      {
+        NSXMLNode *ns = [NSXMLNode namespaceWithName: [aname substringFromIndex: 6]
+                                         stringValue: [attribute stringValue]];
+        [self addNamespace: ns];
+        return;
+      }
+  }
+
   if (attr->ns != NULL)
     {
       xmlNsPtr ns = attr->ns;
diff --git a/Source/NSXMLNode.m b/Source/NSXMLNode.m
